        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "916612c1-5306-52c2-b03e-11cd1470a2d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Royle Family, Half the World Away\n- People: Sue Johnston, Ricky Tomlinson, Caroline Aherne, Ralf Little, Craig Cash\n- Companies: ITV Studios, BBC, Channel 4, ITV\n- Places: Manchester\n- Topics: British television sitcoms, theme tunes\n\nFacts:\n- The Royle Family is a British television sitcom produced by ITV Studios for the BBC that ran for three series from 1998 to 2000.\n- Sue Johnston played Sheila Grant in the Channel 4 soap opera Brookside from 1982 to 1990.\n- The Royle Family returned with specials from 2006 to 2012.\n- The Royle Family centers on a scruffy, television-fixated Manchester family called the Royles.\n- In The Royle Family, Ricky Tomlinson plays family patriarch Jim Royle, Sue Johnston plays Barbara Royle, Caroline Aherne plays Denise Royle, Ralf Little plays Antony Royle, and Craig Cash plays Denise’s fiancé and later husband David.\n- Sue Johnston, born Susan Wright on 7 December 1943, is an English actress.\n- Sue Johnston played Barbara Royle in the BBC comedy The Royle Family from 1998 to 2012.\n- Sue Johnston played Grace Foley in the BBC drama Waking the Dead from 2000 to 2011.\n- Sue Johnston played Gloria Price in the ITV soap opera Coronation Street from 2012 to 2014.\n- Sue Johnston played Miss Denker in the ITV drama Downton Abbey from 2014 to 2015.\n- Half the World Away is well known as the theme tune to the BBC sitcom The Royle Family.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d8026c0a-ec4c-5203-bad6-42e01c40a1a3",
        "text": "Page: The Royle Family. Sentence: The Royle Family is a British television sitcom produced by ITV Studios for the BBC, which ran for three series from 1998-2000, and specials from 2006-12.\nPage: The Royle Family. Sentence: It centres on the lives of a scruffy television-fixated Manchester family, the Royles, comprising family patriarch Jim Royle (Ricky Tomlinson), his wife Barbara (Sue Johnston), their daughter Denise (Caroline Aherne), their son Antony (Ralf Little) and Denise's fiancé (later husband) David (Craig Cash).\nPage: Sue Johnston. Sentence: Sue Johnston OBE (born Susan Wright; born 7 December 1943) is an English actress known for playing Sheila Grant in the Channel 4 soap opera \"Brookside\" (1982–1990), Barbara Royle in the BBC comedy \"The Royle Family\" (1998–2012), Grace Foley in the BBC drama \"Waking the Dead\" (2000–2011), Gloria Price in the ITV soap opera \"Coronation Street\" (2012–2014) and Miss Denker in the ITV drama \"Downton Abbey\" (2014–2015).\nPage: Half the World Away. Sentence: It is well known as the theme tune to the popular BBC sitcom \"The Royle Family\".",
